==============================================================================
N-011  DBSCAN border chaining: a point reachable only through a border
==============================================================================
  prices=[0.0, 0.5, 1.0, 2.0, 2.9] eps=1.0 min_pts=3
  standard-DBSCAN CORE points: [0.0, 0.5, 1.0, 2.0]
  2.0 has 3 neighbours (BORDER);
  2.9 has 2 neighbours and is NOT within eps of any core point -> standard DBSCAN: NOISE
  engine cluster -> [0.0, 0.5, 1.0, 2.0, 2.9]
  engine included 2.9 (a NOISE point) ? True
  -> the BFS re-derives l2/r2 for EVERY dequeued member, so 2.0 (border)
     expands its own neighbourhood and pulls 2.9 into the cluster.

